course: dictionary
lesson: 15127
title: Homo sapiens, the wise human
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists give every living thing a two-part name. The first part is the group, and the second part is the kind. Modern humans are called Homo sapiens. Homo means human, and sapiens is Latin for wise or knowing.
explain: «Sapiens» is an adjective in Latin, so it describes something. In the name Homo sapiens, it tells us which human we are: the wise one. People often shorten it to «sapiens» on its own, and then it is a noun that means modern humans, as in «early sapiens».
explain: Sapiens is not an ordinary English word, so you will not find it in everyday books. When you see it in a science or history lesson, look for Homo just before it. Together they name our own kind of human.
fact: Sapiens is a Latin word meaning «wise» or «knowing».
fact: Homo sapiens means «wise human» and is the scientific name for modern humans.
fact: Homo sapiens appeared in Africa about 300,000 years ago.
fact: Other kinds of humans have their own names, such as Homo neanderthalensis for the Neanderthals.
fact: «Early Homo sapiens» means the first modern humans, who lived long ago.
exercise: The scientific name Homo sapiens means «wise human». What does sapiens mean? | Tiny | Strong and fast | *Wise or knowing | Far away
exercise: «Early Homo sapiens lived in Africa about 300,000 years ago.» Where did they first appear? | Asia | Australia | *Africa | Europe
exercise: The Neanderthals are named Homo neanderthalensis. Which name is for modern humans? | *Homo sapiens | Homo wise | Homo old | Homo neanderthalensis
test: «The museum shows how early sapiens lived.» What does sapiens mean here? | A type of dog | A big stone | *Modern humans | A kind of cloud
test: In the name Homo sapiens, which word means human? | *Homo | Modern | Wise | Sapiens
exam: What does the phrase «early Homo sapiens» mean? | *The first modern humans | A kind of wise owl | Humans who lived only in Scotland | Animals that lived in the sea
